// ───────────── 2.7.1: who is really in the scene ─────────────
// The panel took everyone the model reported in a reply (a mind, a relation, a present-characters line) as standing in
// the room. A living-world bot keeps the absent busy too, so it reports a mind or an agenda for someone far away
// (Beatrice in her library while you stand in the capital's market) and she showed up as a person in the scene.
// Someone is "away" when the reply's own prose never names them AND either their agenda puts them somewhere the HUD's
// ◆ line is not, or the reply's present-characters list leaves them out. No prose to go by: nobody is taken out.
const SCENE_GENERIC = new Set(['room', 'rooms', 'hall', 'house', 'home', 'street', 'road', 'square', 'city', 'town', 'village', 'district', 'floor', 'building', 'tower',
    'manor', 'mansion', 'castle', 'capital', 'kingdom', 'near', 'outside', 'inside', 'front', 'back', 'area', 'place', 'shop', 'store', 'yard', 'with', 'from', 'their', 'somewhere', 'world']);
